 "result_text": "I fixed the duplicate `[None]` sections, but I haven't run the tool or any tests.\n\nWhen no profile was set (no `--profile` and no `$AWS_PROFILE`), the profile name was `None`. `_store` then wrote it out as a literal `[None]` section in the credentials and config files. The first run made one, and the config parser raised `DuplicateSectionError` on a later run.\n\nIn `aws_google_auth/__init__.py`, the credentials are now only stored when a profile is set. With no profile, the tool prints the `export ...` line and writes nothing to disk.\n\nThe catch is that a run with no profile no longer saves anything under `~/.aws`. Before, it also wrote a bogus `[None]` entry there. If you'd rather save such runs under `default`, that is a different change.\n\nAn existing `~/.aws/credentials` that already has two `[None]` sections will stay broken. Delete the `[None]` sections by hand.",
